+### Capture behavior 
+
+MobilePay supports manual and partial capture. A partial capture is final: Stripe releases the uncaptured remainder, and you can’t make a second capture for it.
+
+### Refunds 
+
+MobilePay doesn’t impose a single payment-method-specific refund deadline. Standard card-network and regional rules determine how long after a payment you can submit a refund. You can issue full or partial refunds through the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md), and you can issue multiple partial refunds provided that their total doesn’t exceed the original payment amount. Funds typically appear within 5–10 business days, depending on the issuer. Shortly after creation, some card refunds can be canceled when the Dashboard offers the **Cancel refund** action.
+
+#### Refund process 
+
+MobilePay refunds are processed through the card used for the original payment. Stripe submits the refund to the card issuer. A refund issued shortly after payment can appear as a reversal, where the original charge disappears rather than a separate credit appearing.
+
+#### Tracking refunds 
+
+Track refunds in the Dashboard or retrieve the [Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) through the API. Listen for `refund.updated` and `refund.failed`. [Verify webhook signatures](https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks.md#verify-events) to confirm that events came from Stripe. If you use IP allowlisting, allow Stripe’s [public IP addresses](https://docs.stripe.com/ips.md). Allow approximately 5–10 business days for a credit to appear, depending on the issuer. If the refund fails, inspect its failure reason and arrange another refund method where necessary.
+
+### Disputes 
+
+#### Dispute process 
+
+MobilePay payments are processed using Visa or Mastercard card transactions. Customers can dispute the underlying card payment with their card issuer. There is no separate MobilePay-specific dispute workflow.
+
+#### Dispute notifications 
+
+Stripe notifies you of a dispute by email, in the Dashboard, and through a `charge.dispute.created` webhook event. The dispute reason and response deadline are available in the Dashboard and on the Dispute object.
+
+#### Responding to disputes 
+
+Respond and submit evidence through Stripe’s [standard card-dispute process](https://docs.stripe.com/disputes/responding.md). The applicable response deadline appears in the Dashboard and in `evidence_details.due_by` on the Dispute object.
+
+#### Dispute outcomes 
+
+The card issuer reviews the evidence and decides the outcome. If you win, Stripe returns the disputed amount to your balance. If you lose, the balance debit becomes permanent.
